<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Okinawa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Okinawa was fought from April to June 1945 between American and Japanese forces on Okinawa, the largest battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-war">Pacific War</a> on Japanese territory. It killed about 100,000 Japanese soldiers and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conscription">conscripts</a>, more than 12,000 Americans and tens of thousands of Okinawan civilians, and destroyed Shuri Castle and much of the island. Okinawa remained under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> administration until 1972.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-okinawa.jpg" alt="Battle of Okinawa" width="320" height="254" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Staff Sergent Walter F. Kleine · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ww2_158.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
